            "review_title": "Review at Thai village Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Tock-ling C\nSingapore, Singapore8 contributions\n0\nAvoid Sharks Fin here. Costly and Tasteless!\nFeb 2025 • Family\nThe setting of the restaurant is classy however the quality of its food cannot match its outside appearance. First of all, diners have to climb a steep spiral staircase to access its first floor restaurant. We unfortunately had an elderly lady in our group who really struggled to climb the stairs.\nUnlike its celebrated Thai Village outlets in Singapore, the menu in HCM City is extremely limited. I opted for two medium orders of sharks fin, their signature dish but was quickly disappointed. The fins were not well cook...you could feel the soft bones of the fin poking your teeth as one bites chews into the fin. And the broth was blend and watery, unlike the thick, flavourful one you would expect. We also had kakong, seafood noodles and they were equally badly fried and presented. The sharks fin meal was supposed to be the hi-light of our many meals in HCM City but it had turned out to be the most expensive and the worse. By the way the mid size sharks fin is about SGD 130.00, marginally more expensive than its counter in Singapore. \nAfter eating sharks fin in Bangkok many times, I had foolishly assume sharks fin will be as good in VN, how wrong could I had been?\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nOver priced sharks fin and other seafood. Drinks, service are good.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten February 16, 2025\nThai Village Restaurant - Vietnam\nDear Tock-ling C,\n\nThank you for your detailed feedback. We're truly sorry your experience didn't meet expectations, from the difficult staircase access for your elderly companion, to the undercooked shark fin and watery broth in our signature dish. This is especially disappointing given the price point, and it's not the standard we aim for.\n\nWe're taking your comments seriously and reviewing both our kitchen preparation and accessibility for guests with mobility needs. We'd welcome the chance to make things right. Thank you for your honesty and Sorry for the late reply.\nRead more\nWritten July 28, 2026\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
