            "review_title": "Review at Thai village Restaurant",
            "review_text": "frank v\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam95 contributions\n0\nGreat concept, but don't expect authentic Thai street food flavours nor prices.\nJul 2016 • Business\nI was glad to know there was another Thai venue in Thao Dien and was exited as I was expecting to get authentic thai street food. But I was soon disappointed: the food is so-so, lacking some authentic thai flavours; the service was unfriendly, I had the feeling I was in a canteen; and overall I did not find it was good value for money: you get street food table/chairs and cutlery, but you pay the price of restaurants. A small bottle of mineral water costs 30K... 6 times the price you get from a shop!? So I don't think I'll be going back there as there a much better places to get good Thai food.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 25, 2016\nThai Village Restaurant - Vietnam\nWe're sorry the food, service, and value didn't meet your expectations. We appreciate you giving us a try and hope to have a chance to improve your experience in the future.\nRead more\nWritten July 28, 2026\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
